Track 2: Did We Dig Too Deep?
- Story & Context: Old Man Tiber, a grizzled foreman from the forgotten Borealis Mine, confessed to the new generation that his crew once chased a particularly rich vein, ignoring the tremors and the strange, mournful thrumming from the deeper rock. He still heard the phantom drumming of their picks on the collapsing rock face, a sound that haunted his sleep, forever questioning the price of their ambition. "There are echoes that no shaft can contain," he rasped, his eyes fixed on the distant, pulsing red warning lights.
